1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
MatchPulse Live runs on Azure Container Apps.
This uses synthetic match events only.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The scenario follows Northbridge City
and Harbor United, seeded and fictional.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Events create evidence-linked insights
for each moment in the match.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Northbridge City opens the scoring
from an accepted synthetic event.

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Replaying the same event does not
change the score or duplicate goals.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Out-of-order events are rejected
without corrupting match state.

7
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Fan mode makes the same verified
moment immediate and clear.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Analyst mode adds the calculation,
inputs, and evidence identifiers.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Broadcaster mode condenses the insight
for a live overlay.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Spanish and French localize the copy
while preserving the same match facts.

11
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Northbridge City wins two-one.
The recap cites accepted event evidence.

12
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Foundry and model calls are disabled.
Fallback remains deterministic.

13
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:55,000
MatchPulse Live: hosted and synthetic.
No live external data is used.
